course: dictionary
lesson: 2738
title: Dirtiness and its meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dirtiness is a noun. It names the state of being dirty, and you can find it by adding -ness to dirty, just as kindness comes from kind. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: In a health lesson, the clue is germs: dirtiness of hands or kitchens spreads germs. In a story, the clue is a messy or poor place. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word to check it still makes sense.
explain: Dirtiness has a second, less common meaning: being unfair or dishonest, as in a dirty trick. Look for clues to see which meaning fits. «Eczema often runs in families... and it is not catching or caused by dirtiness.» Here the clue is "not caused by", so dirtiness is named as something that does not cause eczema.
fact: Dirtiness is a noun for the state of being dirty.
fact: «Dirtiness» means being covered in mud, dust or germs.
fact: «Dirtiness» can also mean being unfair or dishonest, as in a dirty trick, but this meaning is less common.
fact: In health lessons, dirtiness of hands or kitchens can spread germs.
fact: «Eczema... is not caused by dirtiness» shows that dirtiness is not the cause of eczema.
exercise: What does dirtiness mean? | *The state of being covered in mud, dust or germs | The state of being quick and light | A loud noise in a room | A kind of happy song
exercise: «Eczema is not catching or caused by dirtiness.» What does this sentence tell you? | Eczema spreads through dirtiness | Dirtiness is the name of an illness | *Dirtiness does not cause eczema | Dirtiness causes eczema
exercise: Which is the less common meaning of dirtiness? | Being covered in mud | *Being unfair or dishonest, as in a dirty trick | Being quick at running | Being very cold
test: In a health lesson, the sentence says «the dirtiness of hands spreads germs». What does dirtiness mean here? | A loud, sudden noise | Being kind and gentle | *Being covered in germs and dirt | Being happy and bright
test: Which word is made by adding -ness to dirty? | *dirtiness | dirtier | dirtily | dirtying
exam: Read this: «Because of its dirtiness, the pond was not safe to swim in.» What clue helps you find the meaning of dirtiness? | The pond was warm, so dirtiness means heat | The pond was big and deep, so dirtiness means size | *The pond was not safe to swim in, so dirtiness means being dirty with mud or germs | The pond had fish, so dirtiness means fishing
